# The engine's own directory, on its parent's: the engine's configuration
# call is variadic in its interface, the one call B22 allows, made in
# sqlite.cpp alone (the structure tests' tokens hold every other file to
# none of SQLite's variadic functions); every other file of the store is
# held to none by its parent's configuration. And SQLite's result codes and
# open flags are ints, its extended codes macros of a signed or and shift,
# which the signed bitwise check reports where they expand: the engine
# alone calls SQLite, and the check stays on in the rest of the store.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >-
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -bugprone-signed-bitwise
